# PawPi web app — environment variable example (NO real secrets here).
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored; this file is committed.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Payments foundation (Phase 2 ticket 2.3) — DO NOT COMMIT REAL KEYS.
#
# The payment layer reads these at runtime. If a rail's keys are UNSET, the payment
# routes return a clean "payments not configured" 503 and never crash — so the app runs
# fine without them until Tats sets up the accounts (sandbox first).
#
# Platform commission, in basis points (100 bps = 1%). Defaults to 0 when unset.
# PLATFORM_COMMISSION_BPS=500
#
# MercadoPago (fiat rail, primary — marketplace / split payments). Create a MercadoPago
# marketplace application (OAuth client) and register the redirect + webhook URLs.
# MP_REDIRECT_URI is a SINGLE FIXED url — it must match, byte-for-byte, the Redirect URL
# registered in the MercadoPago app. It is the provider-facing return PAGE (which reads
# ?code=&state= and completes the per-provider connect); the provider id travels in the
# OAuth `state`, NOT in this url. Do NOT point it at the /api/.../callback route.
# MP_CLIENT_ID=
# MP_CLIENT_SECRET=
# MP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# MP_REDIRECT_URI=https://<your-domain>/provider/payments/mercadopago/return
#
# Binance Pay (crypto rail — merchant QR/deeplink + USDT settlement + Payout API).
# Create a Binance Pay merchant account and generate API key/secret.
# BINANCE_PAY_API_KEY=
# BINANCE_PAY_API_SECRET=
#
# Payment-token encryption-at-rest (Phase 2 ticket 2.16). A 32-byte symmetric key used to
# AES-256-GCM encrypt provider OAuth tokens (MercadoPago access/refresh) BEFORE they are
# stored. Accepts 64 hex chars OR base64 of 32 bytes. Generate one with, e.g.:
#   openssl rand -base64 32      (or:  openssl rand -hex 32)
# MUST be set BEFORE the first real provider connects a payment account (until then the
# connect flow returns a clean 503; existing plaintext rows still decrypt via passthrough).
# Keep it stable — rotating it makes previously-encrypted tokens unreadable. NEVER COMMIT A REAL VALUE.
# PAYMENTS_TOKEN_KEY=
#
# Shop auto-reorder scheduler (Phase 2 ticket 2.17). A shared secret guarding the
# machine-to-machine charge endpoint POST /api/payments/subscriptions/run. PawPi has NO
# built-in scheduler: wire an EXTERNAL one (host cron / scheduled job / CI cron) to POST that
# route daily with the header `x-cron-secret: <this value>`. If unset, the endpoint returns a
# clean 503 ("scheduler not configured") and never runs. NEVER COMMIT A REAL VALUE.
# CRON_SECRET=
#
# Telehealth video vendor (Phase 2 ticket 2.18) — DORMANT behind keys, exactly like payments.
# The consult-join route mints a room via a vendor-agnostic seam (apps/web/.../utils/video).
# If the keys are unset, joining a consult returns a clean 503 ("Video consults aren't set up
# yet") — consults still book + show the join button, nothing crashes. VIDEO_PROVIDER selects
# the adapter (default 'generic'); swap in a real Daily/Jitsi/Twilio adapter without touching
# the routes. NEVER COMMIT REAL VALUES.
#
# Real vendor: Daily.co (set VIDEO_PROVIDER=daily). Daily's REST API auth is a SINGLE API key
# used as a Bearer token — set ONLY VIDEO_API_KEY, no VIDEO_API_SECRET needed for this
# provider (unlike the 'generic' placeholder's original two-key shape, still required for
# 'generic'). Sign up at daily.co, create an API key, set the two vars below on Railway.
# VIDEO_PROVIDER=generic
# VIDEO_API_KEY=
# VIDEO_API_SECRET=
# VIDEO_BASE_URL=https://<your-video-vendor-domain>
#
# Provider enrichment (Phase 2 ticket 2.21) — DORMANT behind keys. "Import from the web" reads
# a provider's links and PROPOSES a draft (the provider confirms before anything is saved). If
# neither key is set, POST /api/providers/<id>/enrich returns a clean 503 ("not set up yet").
# GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY = Google Places Details (hours/address/phone/photos).
# ENRICHMENT_LLM_KEY    = an LLM used to STRUCTURE messy website text into candidate services.
# GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=
# ENRICHMENT_LLM_KEY=
#
# Pet-document ingestion (night-run 2026-08-18d) — DORMANT behind a key. Upload a photo/PDF to the
# Vet Record → Claude vision reads it and PROPOSES structured records the owner confirms before
# anything is saved. Unset → POST /api/vet-record/documents/extract returns a clean 503 ("not set up
# yet"); uploads still store + download and manual record-add still works. ANTHROPIC_MODEL is
# optional (defaults to a current vision-capable Claude that reads images AND PDFs). NEVER COMMIT A
# REAL KEY.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
#
# Web provider-location map pin (Phase 2 ticket 2.81) — OPTIONAL. A browser Google Maps JS API key
# that powers the interactive pin in the web provider Locations form. Unset → the form degrades to
# manual lat/lng inputs (no crash, no key shipped). The MOBILE pin uses Apple Maps (no key needed).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_BROWSER_KEY=
#
# Social sign-in (Phase 2 ticket 2.46) — ADDITIVE + ENV-GATED. A provider is enabled ONLY
# when BOTH its keys are set; with neither set, login is exactly as today (email/password)
# and the "Continue with Google/Apple" buttons stay in their disabled "Coming soon" state —
# no one can be locked out. The existing Credentials path is never affected. NEVER COMMIT
# REAL VALUES.
#
# Register these callback (redirect) URLs with each provider's console:
#   <origin>/api/auth/callback/google
#   <origin>/api/auth/callback/apple
#
# Google: create an OAuth 2.0 Client (Web application) in Google Cloud Console.
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=<google-oauth-client-id>
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=<google-oauth-client-secret>
#
# Apple: create a Services ID (this is AUTH_APPLE_ID) + a Sign in with Apple key (download
# its .p8 once — Apple only lets you download it ONCE). PREFERRED: give the app the raw key
# material and it generates+signs the client-secret JWT itself on every request (N6), so it
# can never silently expire the way a hand-pasted static JWT would within Apple's ~6-month cap:
# AUTH_APPLE_ID=<apple-services-id>
# AUTH_APPLE_TEAM_ID=<apple-developer-team-id>
# AUTH_APPLE_KEY_ID=<sign-in-with-apple-key-id>
# AUTH_APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=<the-.p8-file-contents-including-BEGIN/END-lines>
#
# Legacy alternative (still supported, but you'd have to regenerate this by hand every ~6
# months): set AUTH_APPLE_SECRET directly to a pre-built client-secret JWT instead of the
# three vars above. Ignored when the three vars above are all set.
# AUTH_APPLE_SECRET=<apple-generated-client-secret-jwt>
#
# Transactional email (password reset) — DORMANT behind keys, same pattern as the video/enrichment
# keys above. Powers the reset link sent by POST /api/account/forgot-password. With EMAIL_API_KEY
# UNSET the whole reset flow still works end to end and nothing 500s — the server just logs the
# intended send ("[email] EMAIL_API_KEY not set — skipping send to …") instead of putting a message
# on the wire, and the screen still shows the same "if that account exists, we sent a link" copy.
# So until this key is set, nobody actually receives a reset email.
#
# EMAIL_API_KEY       = the vendor API key. Default vendor is Resend (resend.com) — create an API
#                       key and verify the sending domain there.
# EMAIL_FROM          = the verified sender on the domain verified in Resend. PawPi owns
#                       **pawpi.info** (NOT pawpi.app) — e.g. "PawPi <no-reply@pawpi.info>".
# EMAIL_PROVIDER      = adapter selector; only 'resend' exists today (the default). Swapping to
#                       Postmark/SES means one more branch in api/utils/email, not a route change.
# EMAIL_REPLY_TO      = where REPLIES go. `EMAIL_FROM` above is send-only — Resend authorizes the
#                       whole verified domain, so no-reply@pawpi.info sends fine with no mailbox
#                       behind it, and a user hitting Reply would write into a void. PawPi has ONE
#                       real mailbox, so this defaults to augusto@pawpi.info. Costs nothing (no
#                       extra seat, no alias, no DNS). Only set it to move replies elsewhere.
# EMAIL_API_BASE_URL  = override the vendor endpoint (tests/self-hosted relays). Rarely needed.
# NEVER COMMIT REAL VALUES.
# EMAIL_API_KEY=
# EMAIL_FROM=PawPi <no-reply@pawpi.info>
# EMAIL_REPLY_TO=augusto@pawpi.info
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend
# EMAIL_API_BASE_URL=https://api.resend.com
#
# APP_BASE_URL — the app's own public origin, used to build absolute links in outgoing email
# (currently the password-reset link). SET THIS IN PRODUCTION: with it unset the link is derived
# from the request's Host header, which an attacker can forge to point a real reset token at their
# own server (host-header poisoning). Locally it can stay unset — dev/LAN origins vary by design.
# APP_BASE_URL=https://pawpi-production.up.railway.app
